IMHO we indeed shouldn't check constants against hardcoded values, but we should keep a test that they are defined. How about this?
```js
test('session related constants are defined', (t) => {
  t.assert.strictEqual(typeof SQLITE_CHANGESET_OMIT, 'number');
  t.assert.strictEqual(typeof SQLITE_CHANGESET_REPLACE, 'number');
  t.assert.strictEqual(typeof SQLITE_CHANGESET_ABORT, 'number');
});
```
